issue_context.body:
### Redis version

7.2.5

### Redisson version

3.38.1

### Redisson configuration

Basic cluster config:

```java
Config config = new Config();
config.useClusterServers()
         .addNodeAddress("redis://127.0.0.1:8000", "redis://127.0.0.1:8001","redis://127.0.0.1:8002",
                "redis://127.0.0.1:8003", "redis://127.0.0.1:8004", "redis://127.0.0.1:8005","redis://127.0.0.1:8006",
                "redis://127.0.0.1:8007", "redis://127.0.0.1:8008", "redis://127.0.0.1:8009");
```

### What is the Expected behavior?

When getting a RSet from the RSetMultimap, I would expect it to be created in the main data structure. Since it isn't created, the following strange behaviour happens:

```java
RedissonClient redisson = Redisson.create(config);

RSetMultimap<String, String> multimap = redisson.getSetMultimap("multi");

String setName = multimap.get("set").getName();
redisson.getSet(setName).add("Hello World");

// Expected: [set] Actual: []
System.out.println(multimap.readAllKeySet());
```

### What is the Actual behavior?

No entry in the main RSetMultimap Redis structure is created.

### Additional information

I would create the entry in the main structure when `multimap.get("set")` happens. 

@mrniko Let me know your opinion on this, I would love to contribute if you also feel this makes sense.

